## Context

Post-merge review of PR #368 (0298). `src/go/update.go` around line 187:
`erg sync --upstream` runs an unshallowed `git fetch <url> HEAD`, which
permanently imports git-erg's whole history into every adopter's `.git`.
Adopters only need one blob from one commit.

Caveat found in review: git rejects `--depth` on the local-path transport
the test fixtures use via `insteadOf`, so the fixtures need a `file://` URL
or the depth flag must be applied only for non-local transports.

Two smaller residues from the same review can ride along, one commit each:
the default path re-executes the freshly installed Linux x86-64 binary on
every platform (`update.go` ~271-277), contradicting
`src/go/assets/integration.md`; gate on GOOS/GOARCH. And `AGENTS.md:39`
promises "no network calls, ever" for a command that runs `git fetch`; the
real guarantee is no embedded HTTP client and a graceful exit 0 offline.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The upstream fetch is shallow (`--depth=1` or equivalent) and a test
      asserts the adopter's `.git` does not gain git-erg's history.
- [x] Fixtures still pass offline (negative control unchanged).
- [x] The post-install self-exec is gated on the host platform.
- [x] `AGENTS.md` states the actual offline guarantee.
- [x] `make check` passes.
